# PR#509: same root cause as fazer-ai/chatwoot#508, and the correction path lives there.
# Two messages sharing a `created_at` (ordinary in imported WhatsApp history, whose timestamps
# carry seconds) cannot be ordered by the stamp. Acknowledging the first excludes the second from
# the receipt, which is right; acknowledging the second then moves no stamp, so its receipt never
# goes out. Dispatching anyway would re-receipt the first one, which the round-2 example pins
# against, because the receipt is asynchronous and the first is still unread when the second call
# builds its scope. Both halves need the composite watermark #508 describes: a message id beside
# the timestamp, compared as (created_at, id). Removing this waiver does not close that issue.
#
# What the caller loses meanwhile is the read tick on the contact's phone for the tied message.
# What it does not lose is correctness in the other direction: no message the operator has not
# seen is ever reported as read.
app/controllers/api/v1/accounts/conversations_controller.rb: Allow receipts to advance across equal-timestamp boundaries  # PR#509
